  "usage_note": "**Effort** is uncountable when it means the energy you use (*a lot of effort*) and countable when it means a single attempt (*her efforts to find a job*). After **effort** in the sense of an attempt, use a to-infinitive: *an effort to save money*.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "I did a big effort to finish on time.",
      "correct": "I made a big effort to finish on time.",
      "note": "**Effort** goes with **make**, not **do**."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "He made an effort for learning Spanish.",
      "correct": "He made an effort to learn Spanish.",
      "note": "Use a to-infinitive after **an effort**."
    }
  ],
